  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::480",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1a4 through a shared pathway involving Fxyd2 and potassium-transporting ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Acetyldigitoxin binds to Fxyd2, which then participates in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, ultimately being participated by Atp1a4. This indicates a potential regulatory or structural interaction between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1a4, possibly through Fxyd2 as a mediator. The high scores in the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple paths pointing to Atp1a4 through different intermediates highlights the complexity of the interaction network, but the core link between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1a4 appears to be mediated by Fxyd2 and its role in potassium transport.",
